adjudication.rationale:
In `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the webhook authentication check compares the provided header value to `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` using `!==`:

```ts
if (req.headers[... ] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403).json({ message: "Invalid webhook secret" });
}
```

This is a direct string equality comparison, not a constant-time comparison (e.g., `crypto.timingSafeEqual`). That pattern can be susceptible to timing side-channels in principle, since many string comparisons may short-circuit on the first mismatching byte/character, enabling an attacker with sufficiently precise timing observations to incrementally guess the secret.
